[
    {
        "content": "<p>Use case: I want to iterate through Lean files in a project with their dependencies.</p>\n<p>Consider this MWE:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"c1\">-- Main.lean</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">main</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IO</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">UInt32</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">unsafe</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">enableInitializersExecution</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">initSearchPath</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">findSysroot</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">sp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">getSrcSearchPath</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">IO</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">println</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s!</span><span class=\"s2\">\"sp: {sp}\"</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fname</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">findLean</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">sp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">`Init</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">IO</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">println</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s!</span><span class=\"s2\">\"Init: {fname}\"</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">return</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">lakefile</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">lean</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lake</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lake</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">DSL</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">package</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">probe</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">lean_lib</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Probe</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span>\n<span class=\"o\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">default_target</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span>\n<span class=\"n\">lean_exe</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">probe</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">root</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">`Main</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">supportInterpreter</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">true</span>\n<span class=\"o\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>This runs without any issues:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Bash\"><pre><span></span><code>lean<span class=\"w\"> </span>--run<span class=\"w\"> </span>Main.lean\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>However, running the executable using <code>lake exe</code> results in an error:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Bash\"><pre><span></span><code>lake<span class=\"w\"> </span>exe<span class=\"w\"> </span>probe\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>which says</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">uncaught</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">exception</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">unknown</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">module</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">prefix</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">'</span><span class=\"n\">Init'</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Is there any way to make <code>lake exe</code> have the same behaviour as <code>lean --run</code> here? I also tried compiling with <code>lake build</code> and invoking the executable with <code>.lake/build/bin/probe</code>, but that gives an error as well.</p>",
        "id": 611569836,
        "sender_full_name": "Leni Aniva",
        "timestamp": 1784512496
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The search path in the <code>lake exe</code> case, as printed out by the script, is (shortened for ease of reading)</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">sp</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">PROJECT</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">~/.</span><span class=\"n\">elan</span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"n\">toolchains</span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"n\">leanprover</span><span class=\"c1\">--lean4---v4.29.1/src/lean/lake, $PROJECT/.lake/build/bin/../src/lean/lake, $PROJECT/.lake/build/bin/../src/lean]</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 611569884,
        "sender_full_name": "Leni Aniva",
        "timestamp": 1784512554
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><code>initSearchPath</code> only influences the <code>.olean</code> search path while the <code>.lean</code> search path is currently hard-coded. It might be worthwhile opening an issue about that inconsistency. Meanwhile, something like this should do roughly what <code>initSearchPath</code> does internally</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Bash\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"nv\">LEAN_SRC_PATH</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"k\">$(</span>lean<span class=\"w\"> </span>--print-prefix<span class=\"k\">)</span>/src/lean\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 611612511,
        "sender_full_name": "Sebastian Ullrich",
        "timestamp": 1784535462
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"110024\">Sebastian Ullrich</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/239415-metaprogramming-.2F-tactics/topic/.60lean.20--run.60.20vs.20.60lake.20exe.60/near/611612511\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p><code>initSearchPath</code> only influences the <code>.olean</code> search path while the <code>.lean</code> search path is currently hard-coded. It might be worthwhile opening an issue about that inconsistency. Meanwhile, something like this should do roughly what <code>initSearchPath</code> does internally</p>\n<p><div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Bash\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"nv\">LEAN_SRC_PATH</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"k\">$(</span>lean<span class=\"w\"> </span>--print-prefix<span class=\"k\">)</span>/src/lean\n</code></pre></div><br>\n</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>it seems like even without this circumvention, <code>findLean</code> can find modules that are not built-in to Lean (<code>Init</code>, <code>Std</code>, <code>Lean</code>)</p>",
        "id": 611961740,
        "sender_full_name": "Leni Aniva",
        "timestamp": 1784659286
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Ah, so maybe the better question/issue report would be why <code>lake env</code> lists those paths but not Lean's own root</p>",
        "id": 612113102,
        "sender_full_name": "Sebastian Ullrich",
        "timestamp": 1784720543
